From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:36:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] AROS: writes to a language server fail once it has
 ended

On AROS One a write to a pipe whose reader has ended does not fail, it
waits. After a language server crashed, the next edit sent it a
didChange; that write never returned, and Tokio waited for it when hx
ended, so hx hung after its terminal was restored (seen on v11: hang
after one edit, clean exit without edits).

ChildStdin and ChildStdout of one child now share a flag: end of file on
the child's stdout marks it ended, and later writes or flushes of its
stdin fail with BrokenPipe at once instead of starting a blocking write.
A write already under way when the child ends is not covered. A child
that closes its stdout but keeps reading stdin would lose its input;
language servers do not do that.

process.rs is now also built for host tests on Unix; two tests cover a
write after the child closed its output and a write to a running child.
